<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sattar Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1868–1914</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sattar Khan was a leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persian-constitutional-revolution">Iranian Constitutional Revolution</a>, a former horse dealer from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabriz">Tabriz</a> who organised the city's defence after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohammad-ali-shah-qajar">Mohammad Ali Shah</a> closed the Majlis in 1908. His fighters held Tabriz against royalist forces for about ten months, keeping the constitutional cause alive until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tehran">Tehran</a> was taken in 1909. Honoured as Sardar-e Melli, the National Commander, he died in Tehran in 1914.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sattar-khan.jpg" alt="Sattar Khan" width="320" height="399" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SattarKhanPortrait.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
